# Keep the build context lean. Without this, `podman build` tar-streams
# the entire monorepo into the builder — including 261 GB of GGUFs and
# multi-GB cargo build outputs — making every container build start
# with a multi-minute "Sending build context" stall.
#
# The Containerfiles under sovereign/container/ COPY in only the paths
# cargo / build-scripts actually need; this list enumerates the bulky
# directories that are NEVER referenced by those COPYs so podman can
# skip them outright.

# Local Rust build artifacts (workspace target + per-crate targets).
target/
**/target/

# 261 GB of GGUFs. The container pulls models from R2 at runtime via
# rclone; the host's local cache must never leak into the image.
sovereign/models/

# The OTHER model cache. `models/` is a distinct, gitignored (.gitignore:98)
# top-level tree of GGUFs and embedding models — 2.1 GB on RuggedFox — and it
# was missed when its `sovereign/models/` sibling above was excluded. Same
# reasoning, same treatment.
models/

# Local research artifacts. `research/verifier-v0` alone is 33 GB of run
# outputs on RuggedFox; the tree is NOT a cargo workspace member and no
# Containerfile references it. This one dominated the miss: measured
# 2026-08-10, the desktop build context was 36 GB, of which research/ was
# 33 GB and models/ 2.1 GB — for an image build whose ONLY COPY is a single
# entrypoint script. Excluding both takes the context to 789 MB (46x).
#
# Why excluding a workspace path is safe here: .containerignore scopes the
# `podman build` CONTEXT only. Neither desktop Containerfile COPYs the
# workspace at all — the build driver bind-mounts the repo at /work at RUN
# time (`-v "$REPO_ROOT:/work:Z"`), so the container still sees every path,
# excluded or not. Trimming the context cannot starve the build.
research/

# Container build OUTPUTS and the isolated caches that feed them. `**/target/`
# matches a directory named exactly "target", so NONE of these are covered by
# the rule above. build-desktop-linux.sh mkdir -p's them so container builds
# don't stomp the host's caches; every one grows without bound.
#
# Caught live 2026-08-10 by release-build-context.sh while the first Linux
# container CLI leg was running: the measured context climbed 716 MB -> 1487 MB
# mid-session as .cargo-container filled with the crates registry, and
# target-container-linux reached 3.5 GB inside one build. This is the same
# defect as research/ above, arriving through a different door — which is the
# argument for the budget check over any list of names.
# GLOBS, not a fixed list. The linux and windows legs create DIFFERENT sets
# (.cargo-container vs .cargo-container-windows, .npm-container-modules vs
# .npm-container-modules-windows), and enumerating them by hand is how the
# windows set came to be missed on the first pass at this file. A glob covers
# the next variant before it exists.
target-container-*/
.cargo-container*/
.npm-container*/
.tauri-cache-container/
.xwin-container/
.ort-cache-container/

# Release outputs. dist/ holds the packaged tarballs plus their .sha256 and
# .buildinfo sidecars — up to four CLI triples per cut, and the bytes we are
# shipping have no business riding along in the context that builds them.
dist/

# ─── Re-included on purpose ───────────────────────────────────────────
# `target/` above is excluded wholesale, but sovereign/container/Containerfile
# .local-test COPYs the host-built release binary OUT of it — that image
# deliberately bakes in a binary compiled on the host rather than rebuilding
# Rust in-image. Without this negation that COPY cannot resolve and the image
# cannot be built at all: measured against podman 5.8.4, the build fails
#
#     Error: building at STEP "COPY target/release/sovereign-cli ...":
#     no items matching glob "..." copied (1 filtered out using
#     .../.containerignore): no such file or directory
#
# exit 125, while the identical build with the exclusion lifted exits 0. The
# conflict had gone unnoticed because that image's only tests are #[ignore]d
# (sovereign-mesh/tests/local_pod_smoke.rs:262,415) and its header asserts the
# opposite — "the build context is the workspace root so this path resolves".
#
# Ordering is load-bearing: `.containerignore` evaluation is last-match-wins,
# so this MUST stay below `target/`. One file, not the tree — and if the
# release binary ever grows enough to matter, the context budget check names it.
!target/release/sovereign-cli

# sovereign-recipes/ is INCLUDED wholesale (≈1.4 MB): corpus-engine's
# build.rs vendors the whole tree into OUT_DIR, and sovereign-contracts
# include_str!s registry.toml + schema/. The tree used to be excluded
# here when multi-GB bench gyms lived in it — those were evicted to
# sovereign/bench by the recipes single-source-of-truth refactor, so
# there is nothing bulky left to skip.

# IDE / editor scratch state.
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Local databases, logs, traces.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
*.log

# Git internals — never needed in the image.
.git/

# Container artifacts themselves.
**/Containerfile
**/Dockerfile
.containerignore
.dockerignore
